# Pre-push quality gate

Before every `git push` (including `-u` / first push of a branch):

1. Run these in order and wait for each to succeed:
   - `npm run lint`
   - `npm run typecheck`
   - `npm run format:check`
   - `npm test`
2. Push only if all four exit 0.
3. If any fail: fix the issues, re-run the failing command, then push. Do not push with `--no-verify`.
4. If uncommitted WIP would make `format:check` fail on files not part of the push, stash it (`git stash push -u -m "pre-push-wip"`), run the four checks, push, then `git stash pop`.

The repo also has `.husky/pre-push` as a hard gate; do not bypass it.
